  "source_sha": "16fb834f1a03a70f165be470a5f98f389bf6100a (dirty working tree, 120 entries; no commit made by this lane)",
  "decision": "CP-106, CP-108 (docs/engineering/DECISIONS.md)",
  "why_this_file_exists": "CP-106 requires the count of task records naming an unachievable verification command to be MEASURED, not estimated, and requires each one to be corrected or explicitly accepted with a recorded reason. This file is that measurement and those reasons, in one discoverable place, so a reader who opens a single stale record can find the disposition without reading 27 records.",
  "measurement_method": {
    "scope": "every .json task record under docs/engineering/tasks/**, excluding TASK_INDEX.json and SCHEMA.json",
    "records_scanned": 183,
    "match": "the record text contains the string `verify:feature`",
    "reproduction": "rg -l 'verify:feature' docs/engineering/tasks --glob '!TASK_INDEX.json' | wc -l",
    "whole_repo_cross_check": "rg -l --hidden -g '!node_modules' -g '!.git' -g '!.next' 'verify:feature' . | wc -l  => 44 files; of those 33 contain the --changed form"
  },
  "headline_counts": {
    "task_records_naming_verify_feature_anywhere": 27,
    "task_records_listing_it_in_verification_commands": 22,
    "task_records_using_the_changed_flag": 24,
    "task_records_citing_CP_106": 3,
    "task_records_never_run_at_all": 18,
    "task_records_with_a_recorded_result": 9,
    "by_status": {
      "active": 11,
      "blocked": 16
    }
  },
  "correction_of_the_orchestrator_estimate": "The task brief said \"roughly 100 task records specify `npm run verify:feature -- --changed`\". That does not reproduce. Measured against docs/engineering/tasks/** the figure is 27 task records containing `verify:feature` at all, 22 listing it in verification.commands, and 20 using the --changed form. The whole-repository figure including work packets, agent STATE files, handoffs and prose is 44 files. The estimate is high by roughly four; the direction of the finding is unchanged, and the measured number is what CP-106 asks for.",
  "disposition_model": "Three buckets. (1) RECOVERED - the record names a command that now runs to a conclusion; nothing to edit, because the command string was never wrong. (2) HISTORICAL - the record states a factually true observation about the tier as it was, with a run timestamp; rewriting it would be falsifying evidence, so it is explicitly accepted and left byte-identical. (3) PER-FILE EDITS - none were made, and the reason is recorded under edits_not_made.",
  "buckets": {
    "recovered_never_run": {
      "count": 18,
